because he loves Christmas.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:11.613
We decorated, we put the Christmas tree

00:01:11.613 --> 00:01:13.780
out all the decorations everywhere.

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:15.360
And we did Christmas in July for like.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.400
a good three weeks almost the whole month.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.710
I feel like you could almost get away

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:20.090
with it in the lockdown at a point

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:21.810
where every day feels the same.

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.280
I couldn't tell you
what the date is today.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:25.950
I feel like if I just
saw Christmas decorations

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:27.984
at the background, I guess
it's as good as Christmas now.

00:01:27.984 --> 00:01:28.817
Yeah.

00:01:28.817 --> 00:01:29.650
They're probably right.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.660
They're probably right, dang it.

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:34.960
Yeah, I miss that too.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.283
That's why we're drinking

00:01:36.283 --> 00:01:38.103
in the middle of the afternoon.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.620
Cheers of drinking that ginger max.

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:42.650
What do you got over there?

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:45.610
Cheers, it seems we have the same cup.

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:46.443
Look at this.

00:01:46.443 --> 00:01:47.444
Yes.

00:01:47.444 --> 00:01:50.770
